\f0\b\fs24 \cf0 Honda S2000 CR and CR Turbo\
\
Update (09/15/2008): Based on comments in the Honda S2000CR post on the Ambrosia web board, the .car was renamed, as were several other files.  The Turbo exhaust fire was modified slightly, as was the  front/rear sway bars on the Turbo.  Basically, the car, in the handling/performance department, is finished. \
\
Update (09/05/2008): Larger brakes were added to Turbo to cope with added power, and stock CR front/rear sway bars were resized for less understeer.  In addition some exhaust flame was added to the Turbo upon shifting at full throttle.
\b0 \
\
This version of Andreu's Honda S2000 is developed from Honda's production-spec S2000 CR (stands for Club Racer).  As such, I decided to eliminate body roll, introduce better tires, a more agressive gearing, and larger front and rear anti-roll bars, so that it is significantly faster and handles better than a stock S2000.   In addition, I modified the engine sound and horn.\
\
In line with the stock S2000 CR, I decided to make a turbo version (as the stock CR has no power increase, and the car practically begged to light up the tires), putting out 402 HP and 302 TQ.  It features the same refinements as the stock S2000 CR, taken to the extreme.  The body roll has by now been completely dialed out, as well as all understeer (it actually tends to light oversteer in a very controlled manner).  Making contact with the road, the turbo features super-grippy racing slicks, giving you, the driver more control.  In fact, this car, during testing, consistently breaks the 1:55 at Monaco, and will go 200 mph on the salt flats.\
\
Please note that The CR is only faster than a S2000 driven by a human in a straight line, because for some reason, a computer driven S2000 normally runs through the quarter mile in 12.2 seconds (the best a real person can do is 13.7 (13.4 for the CR)).  The Turbo turns a 11.8 quarter.\
